    "result_text": "There's only the one test class, and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 telephone for humans while leaving the raw `telephone` in E.164 form.\n\nFollowing the project's existing pattern for derived owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, etc. \u2014 `@Transient` getters on the `Owner` entity, exposed through the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` and auto-mapped by MapStruct), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it by name.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTelephoneDisplay()` getter. It splits the stored E.164 value into country code + national digits (recognizing `+61` and `+1`, defaulting to a two-digit country code otherwise), then regroups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. It returns `null` when no telephone is set or the value isn't E.164, and leaves `getTelephone()` untouched.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
